"Simple Brayton cycle: open gas turbine with air, states 1 to 4

 Compressor 1 -> 2, combustor 2 -> 3 (modelled as a heater), turbine 3 -> 4. Air is a real fluid
 from CoolProp (Lemmon et al., 2000), so cp varies with temperature and pressure.

 Also in this project:
   Cycle diagram   compressor, combustor, turbine and generator on one shaft
   Parametric      efficiency and specific work over the pressure ratio
   Plots           T-s diagram, and efficiency and specific work against the pressure ratio
   Optimisation    pressure ratio that maximises the specific work"

"The unit system: C, bar, kJ, kg/s"
$UnitSystem Eng

"---------------------------------------------------------------- inputs"
T[1] = 15 [C];  P[1] = 1.013 [bar]     // ISO ambient
r_p = 12                       "compressor pressure ratio"
dp_cc = 0.03                   "combustor pressure loss (fraction of its inlet pressure)"
T[3] = 1100 [C]                "turbine inlet temperature"
eta_c = 0.86                   "compressor isentropic efficiency"
eta_t = 0.89                   "turbine isentropic efficiency"
m_dot = 20 [kg/s]              "air mass flow"

P[2] = r_p*P[1]
P[3] = P[2]*(1 - dp_cc)
P[4] = P[1]                    // the turbine exhausts to ambient pressure

"Mass flow of every state (the fuel flow is neglected)"
Duplicate i = 1, 4
  m[i] = m_dot
End

"---------------------------------------------------------------- states"
h[1] = enthalpy(Air, T=T[1], P=P[1])
s[1] = entropy(Air, T=T[1], P=P[1])

"Compressor 1 -> 2"
h_s[2] = enthalpy(Air, P=P[2], s=s[1])
eta_c = (h_s[2] - h[1]) / (h[2] - h[1])
T[2] = temperature(Air, P=P[2], h=h[2])
s[2] = entropy(Air, P=P[2], h=h[2])

"Turbine 3 -> 4"
h[3] = enthalpy(Air, T=T[3], P=P[3])
s[3] = entropy(Air, T=T[3], P=P[3])
h_s[4] = enthalpy(Air, P=P[4], s=s[3])
eta_t = (h[3] - h[4]) / (h[3] - h_s[4])
T[4] = temperature(Air, P=P[4], h=h[4])
s[4] = entropy(Air, P=P[4], h=h[4])

"---------------------------------------------------------------- performance"
W_c = m[1]*(h[2] - h[1])       {kW}
W_t = m[3]*(h[3] - h[4])       {kW}
Q_in = m[2]*(h[3] - h[2])      {kW}
W_net = W_t - W_c              {kW}
eta_th = W_net/Q_in            "thermal efficiency"
w_spec = W_net/m_dot           {kJ/kg}  "specific work (names are case-insensitive: w_net would be W_net)"
bwr = W_c/W_t                  "back-work ratio"

"Ideal (air-standard, constant cp) efficiency for comparison: 1 - r_p^(-(k-1)/k)"
k = cp(Air, T=T[1], P=P[1])/cv(Air, T=T[1], P=P[1])
eta_ideal = 1 - r_p^(-(k - 1)/k)
